Precheck that the nova_libvirt image ships kolla_nova_libvirt_start.

The virtlogd change switched the nova_libvirt container command to
/usr/local/bin/kolla_nova_libvirt_start, a helper that launches
libvirtd alongside virtlogd so guest console logs are rotated. That
helper only exists in matching nova-libvirt images.

A deployer who upgrades Kolla-Ansible but keeps an older
nova_libvirt image (an incomplete upgrade) would end up with a
container that cannot start, because the configured command is not
present in the image. Add a deploy-time check that inspects the
nova_libvirt image for the helper and fails with an explanatory
message when it is absent, so the misconfiguration is caught before
the container is reconfigured rather than surfacing as a confusing
container start failure.

The check runs from version-check.yml, which deploy.yml imports
before the container is (re)configured, and can be bypassed with the
nova-libvirt-script-check tag for deployers who knowingly run an
older image.

